.TH SUDO 8 "2026-08-16" "notcoreutils" "notcoreutils Manual"
.SH NAME
sudo \- minimal, doas-style privilege escalation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo
\fICMD\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sudo
prompts for your own password and, if you are a member of the
.I wheel
group, execs CMD as root.
.PP
Deliberately doas\-sized, not sudo\-sized: no /etc/sudoers file or
rule grammar, no per\-command matching, no session/timestamp caching
(every invocation re\-prompts \- a deliberate choice, not a missing
feature: no cached\-auth window for another process on the same tty
to ride), no NOPASSWD, no logging pipeline. One group check, one
password check, one exec.
.SH INSTALLATION
Must be installed setuid\-root to work at all:
.RS
.nf
chown root:root sudo
chmod 4755 sudo
.fi
.RE
Refuses cleanly, with a clear error, if it is not.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR su (1)
